<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trần Quý Khoáng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1414</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Trùng Quang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trần Quý Khoáng, known by his reign name Trùng Quang, was the second and last emperor of the Later Trần dynasty, which resisted the Ming occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. He was proclaimed in 1409 by followers of the generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dang-tat">Đặng Tất</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-canh-chan">Nguyễn Cảnh Chân</a>, whom the first Later Trần emperor, Giản Định, had executed. He fought the Ming armies of Zhang Fu in central Vietnam until his capture in 1414, and died on the way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div>
